  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth - RLC - Afri-Sandals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afri-Sandal is social enterprise and investment fund that generates revenues through making sandals out of waste materials such as used vehicle tires, leather boards, Africa beadwork and used fabric and old jeans. The sandals are produced by persons with disability sold the revenues earned are re-invested in building an investment fund that offers financing and training to women with disability having viable business ideas to launch off their social ventures and repay back the money with an interest of 2% while they get 1:1 mentorship and connection to other business opportunities to growth their social ventures for significant social impact.</narrative>
  </description>
